# The rclone-manager-tests commit this repository's gate runs its browser
# e2e suite and its CLI smoke slice from. Moved by
# scripts/e2e/bump-tests-pin.sh, and the commit that moves it is itself
# gated against the new pin, so a bad bump cannot land unnoticed.
#
# Why this repository pins that one, and that one pins a build of this one:
# pinning the tests repository means a new or changed test cannot break
# unrelated in-flight work here until someone bumps this line, and the bump
# is itself gated. Pinning the product build over there means a release
# cannot silently change what those suites certify. Each is one line, in one
# file, reviewable on its own.
#
# This line was deliberately held at 9dfd6e3 by #409 while #240's Suite B
# specs (0f89776, "Prove Suite B can see where a backup's copies are") sat
# over there ahead of the feature: eighteen browser cases that put an
# artifact's placements on screen, 17 of which are red against a product
# that has no such surface. That is the arrangement working as designed,
# and #240 is the pull request that makes them true, so it is the one that
# moves the pin: to that repository's main, which is 0f89776 plus the
# equivalence-matrix work from #376 (778891a) and its verb-name correction
# (71e303f). Nothing in the later two touches what this gate runs, since
# both live in suites/equivalence (Suite C) and this gate runs Suite A's
# smoke slice and Suite B, never Suite C.
TESTS_REPO_URL=https://github.com/spdrman/rclone-manager-tests.git
TESTS_REPO_SHA=71e303fbb81e4d7ca94cc4833e716559a019092e
